              "\"The move clearly shows that 25% is not a ceiling on tariffs and thus must increase materially the uncertainty about the outlook for the trade war for businesses,\" wrote Seth Carpenter, chief US economist at UBS.\n\nAs tariffs have mounted, economic challenges have grown, wrote Carpenter. Data show that imports of goods have fallen 40% because of tariffs, and domestic spending has been consistently weak since tariffs were enacted last year, he said",
